== 3. what this run does and does not show ==
   Shows: the DUT asserts rvfi_ext_irq_valid in a cycle where rvfi_valid is also high, the offending term of
   every firing being the (!rvfi_valid) half, so the flag is not spurious and a retirement really is coincident.
   Does not show: the cycle-level detail (which instruction's writeback completed, whether the four-cycle offset
   from the notification pulse holds). No waveform was dumped by this build: the local runner compiles
   -debug_access+pp and has no dump option. A shape-matched wave was produced separately in a scratch root with
   -debug_access+all and the flow's gen_dump.tcl, reproducing eleven firings and the same first cycle.
